# Accent / Brand Theming

UI chrome that follows the user’s accent preference **must** use the theme tokens — never hardcode brand reds/greens for chrome.

## Tokens (themable)

| Token | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `--accent` | Primary brand accent |
| `--accent-2` | Lighter accent (text / soft highlights) |
| `--accent-bright` | Mid step for gradients |
| `--accent-ink` | Foreground on solid accent fills |
| `--brand` | Primary gradient (`bright → accent`) |

Applied at runtime by `frontend/src/accent-theme.ts` from Settings → Allgemein → Akzentfarbe (`localStorage` key `agravion.accentTheme`).

## Do

- Style brand chrome with `var(--accent)`, `var(--accent-2)`, `var(--accent-bright)`, `var(--accent-ink)`, `var(--brand)`.
- Mix neutrals for dark washes: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 20%, #121416)` — not red-tinted hexes like `#1a0c0e`.
- Add new brand UI (nav active, focus rings, primary CTAs, selection chrome, progress fills tied to brand) only through these tokens.

## Do not theme (semantic status)

Keep fixed green / warning / danger for state meaning:

- `--ok`, `--ok-2`, `--online` — positive status (Online, Aktiv, Ja, Starten / `btn-ok`, ready)
- `--warning`, `--danger`, `--offline`

Crop/map/fuel/weather domain colors stay domain-specific.

## Custom & presets

Presets and custom hex live in `accent-theme.ts`. Extending presets means adding an entry there **and** i18n labels under `settings.accentPreset*`.
